[INFO|base_episode_generator.py:176:154] 2026-10-26 06:41:31,921 >> The first step in polynomial long division is to divide the leading term of the dividend by the leading term of the divisor. So, the leading term of the dividend is \(2x^4\), and the leading term of the divisor is \(x^2\). Dividing those gives \(2x^4 / x^2 = 2x^2\). So, the first term of the quotient is \(2x^2\).
